  <category>
    <pattern>DEFINE OMPHALOPTICK</pattern>
    <template>An optickglassthat is convex on both fides, commonly called a con- vex lens. ON, on', prep. It is put besore the word, which (ignisies that which is under, that by which any thing is. fupported, wiich any thing covers, or where any thing is fixed; noting addition or accumulation, as mil- chiess On mischiess ; noting a ftate of progresiicn, as whither On thy way ? noting dependance or reli- ance, as On God's providence their hopes depend; at, noting place; it denotes the motive or occasion of any thing ; it denotes the time at which any thing happens, as this happened On the firll day; in forms of denunciation it is put besore the thing threatened ; noting invoca- tion ; noting flipulation or condi- tion. ON, on', ad. Forward, in fucceslion ; forward, in progreslion ; in conti- nuance, without cealing; upon the body, as part of dress; it notes re- folution to advance. ON, on', interjed. A word of incite- ment or encouragement.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS OMPHALOPTICK</pattern>
