    <pattern>DEFINE PRECIPICE</pattern>
    <template>Ahead- long deep, a fall perpendicular. PRECIPITANCE, pre-slp'-py- tens. PRECIPITANCY, pre tlp'-py- ten-fy. Ralli haste, headlong hade. PREClPiT.ANT, pre-sip'-py-tcnt. a. Falling or rulhing headlong; hally, urged with violent halle ; rashly hurried. PRECIPITANTLY, presip'-py- tent-l)'. ad. In headlong halle, in a tumultuous hurry. ToPRECIPrrATE,pre-!lp'-p;^-tate. V. a. To throw headlong, to hallen unexpcstedly ; to hurry blindly or rashly; to throw to the bottom, a term of chymiliry opposed to Sub- lime. ToPRECIPITATE,prc-5ip'-p)--ia:e. V. n. To fall headlong; to fall to the bottom as a fediment; to hallen without jull preparation.</template>
  </category>
